  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Restore Habitat for Cao Vit Gibbons</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Cao Vit Gibbon is one of the world&apos;s most endangered primates. It is currently found only along the border between China and Vietnam, with an estimated 130 individuals in the wild. Gibbons are highly dependent on trees for their survival. Therefore, in order to protect them, Shanghai Roots &amp; Shoots plans to restore their only habitat in China that has been previously destroyed by human activities by planting trees to provide them with food and habitat.</narrative>
  </description>
